        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Simplify the expression <span class=\"math\">[MATH: - \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Simplify the expression [MATH: - \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we rewrite the negative sign as multiplication by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (-1)\\mathbin:]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n- \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&amp;=\\\n(-1) \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)\n}]</span></p><p>Then, we distribute the <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (-1)]</span> to each term in the parentheses, and simplify:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(-1) \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&amp;=\\\n(-1) (3n)+(-1) \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&amp;=\\\n-3n+ \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right) &amp;=\\\n-3n-\\dfrac{1}{2}k\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we rewrite the negative sign as multiplication by [MATH: (-1)\\mathbin:]\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n- \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&=\\\n(-1) \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)\n}]\n\nThen, we distribute the [MATH: (-1)] to each term in the parentheses, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(-1) \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&=\\\n(-1) (3n)+(-1) \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&=\\\n-3n+ \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right) &=\\\n-3n-\\dfrac{1}{2}k\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: - \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we rewrite the negative sign as multiplication by [MATH: (-1)\\mathbin:]\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n- \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&=\\\n(-1) \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)\n}]\n\nThen, we distribute the [MATH: (-1)] to each term in the parentheses, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(-1) \\left( 3n+\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&=\\\n(-1) (3n)+(-1) \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right)&=\\\n-3n+ \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2}k \\right) &=\\\n-3n-\\dfrac{1}{2}k\n}]"
      },
