          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we rewrite the negative sign as multiplication by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (-1)\\mathbin:]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n-(2x-1.3)&amp;=\\\n(-1)(2x-1.3)\n}]</span></p><p>Then, we distribute the <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (-1)]</span> to each term in the parentheses, and simplify:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(-1)(2x-1.3)&amp;=\\\n(-1) (2x)-(-1) (1.3)&amp;=\\\n-2x-(-1.3)&amp;=\\\n-2x+1.3\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we rewrite the negative sign as multiplication by [MATH: (-1)\\mathbin:]\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n-(2x-1.3)&=\\\n(-1)(2x-1.3)\n}]\n\nThen, we distribute the [MATH: (-1)] to each term in the parentheses, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(-1)(2x-1.3)&=\\\n(-1) (2x)-(-1) (1.3)&=\\\n-2x-(-1.3)&=\\\n-2x+1.3\n}]",
